WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.590
A kosher café.

2
00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.910
On the menu: a beef burger.

3
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.470
A cheese toastie.

4
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.130
Both are kosher.

5
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:11.340
Now put that same beef and
that same cheese in one bun.

6
00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.400
The café cannot serve it.

7
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.060
Kosher means fit, or proper.

8
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.090
For many Jews, these food laws
shape every meal of the day.

9
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.160
So how can two kosher foods
make one dish that is not?

10
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.610
In this mission, you'll sort
animals the way the Torah does:

11
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.420
hoofs and cud, fins and scales.

12
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.380
Then you'll step inside a kosher kitchen
and see how a family organises it.

13
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.170
Your mission: find out why a kosher
café can't serve a cheeseburger,

14
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.150
even when both the beef
and the cheese are kosher.
